    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0664" n="532" xml:id="pg532"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/7–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 371<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the
                        Representative on the Allied Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-08T14:00:00-04:00">July 8, 1945—2 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1557. For Pauley.</p>
                <p>Instead of replying now to the questions raised in your 2418, July 5, 8
                        p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d371-f1"/> Secretary suggests that these issues be
                    discussed and decided when you join President at Berlin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed><anchor n="2" xml:id="d371-f2"/>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d371-f1" n="1" xml:id="d371-f1-content">
